  "gloss": "to freeze hard; to be frozen",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to freeze hard; to be frozen",
      "explanation": "To freeze solid in bitter cold. A literary word, used mostly in descriptions of winter cold, roads and air."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "32621_itetsuku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{凍|い}てつく⟦{寒|さむ}さ→寒さ：12336_samusa⟧だった。",
      "english": "It was bitterly, freezingly cold.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "32621_itetsuku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{凍|い}てついた⟦{道|みち}→道：00505_michi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{歩|ある}く→歩く：00538_aruku⟧。",
      "english": "To walk along a frozen road.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "32621_itetsuku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{凍|い}てつくような⟦{冬|ふゆ}→冬：00623_fuyu⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{朝|あさ}→朝：02277_asa⟧、⟦{湖|みずうみ}→湖：00867_mizuumi⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧⟦{一面|いちめん}→一面：11184_ichimen⟧⟦{氷|こおり}→氷：02753_koori⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{覆|おお}われていた→覆う：02020_oou⟧。",
      "english": "On a freezing winter morning, the lake was covered with ice from shore to shore.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Literary and descriptive; in conversation people say ⟦{凍|こお}る→凍る：02100_kooru⟧ or ものすごく⟦{寒|さむ}い→寒い：00664_samui⟧. Mostly in the forms {凍|い}てつく and {凍|い}てついた before a noun.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {凍|い}てつく⟦{寒|さむ}さ→寒さ：12336_samusa⟧: freezing cold\n- {凍|い}てつく⟦{夜|よる}→夜：00487_yoru⟧: a freezing night\n- {凍|い}てついた⟦{大地|だいち}→大地：12187_daichi⟧: the frozen ground\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{凍|こお}る→凍る：02100_kooru⟧: to freeze; the everyday word\n- ⟦{凍|こご}える→凍える：09124_kogoeru⟧: to be numb with cold (of people and hands)",
